  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. machinery exports were $283.61B in 2025 (+12.4%); the largest headings were computers (8471, $61.18B), computer parts (8473, $35.76B), semiconductor equipment (8486, $19.27B).",
    "Mexico and Canada took 41% of exports; Mexico and the free-trade partners charge nothing on qualifying goods, and the EU went to zero on July 1, 2026.",
    "Canada has surtaxed about 50 machinery tariff items at 15%, 25% or 50% since September 8, 2026 — air conditioners, refrigerators, washers, lifting equipment and parts — and CUSMA qualification does not remove it.",
    "China adds a 10% extra duty on all U.S. goods and another 10% on agricultural machinery; U.S. machine tools, chip-making equipment and some pumps and valves also need U.S. export licences for some destinations."
  ],
